      {
        "question_text": "Write all factor pairs of $48$, then list all its factors in ascending order.",
        "solution_text": "$1 \\times 48=48$\n$2 \\times 24=48$\n$3 \\times 16=48$\n$4 \\times 12=48$\n$48 \\div 5=9$ remainder $3$, so $5$ is not a factor.\n$6 \\times 8=48$\n$48 \\div 7=6$ remainder $6$, so $7$ is not a factor.\n$8 \\times 6$ reverses the pair $6 \\times 8$, so there are no more new pairs.\nThe factors are $1,2,3,4,6,8,12,16,24,48$."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Is $2$ a factor of $38$?\nIs $5$ a factor of $38$?\nShow how you know.",
        "solution_text": "$38 \\div 2=19$\nThere is no remainder, so $2$ is a factor of $38$.\n$38 \\div 5=7$ remainder $3$.\nThere is a remainder, so $5$ is not a factor of $38$."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Complete the factor pair $6 \\times \\square=78$.",
        "solution_text": "$78 \\div 6=13$\n$6 \\times 13=78$\nThe missing factor is $13$."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "List all factors of $81$ and state how many there are.\nExplain why one factor pair uses the same factor twice.",
        "solution_text": "$1 \\times 81=81$\n$3 \\times 27=81$\n$9 \\times 9=81$\nThe pair $9 \\times 9$ uses the same factor twice because multiplying $9$ by itself gives $81$.\nInclude $9$ only once in the factor list.\nThe factors are $1,3,9,27,81$.\nThere are $5$ factors."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Fill in the gaps to complete the factors of $54$: $1,\\square,3,\\square,9,\\square,27,54$.",
        "solution_text": "$1 \\times 54=54$\n$2 \\times 27=54$\n$3 \\times 18=54$\n$6 \\times 9=54$\nThe missing factors are $2,6,18$.\nThe complete list is $1,2,3,6,9,18,27,54$."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "A student lists the factors of $20$ as $1,2,5,10,20$.\nFind the missing factor and correct the list.",
        "solution_text": "$1 \\times 20=20$\n$2 \\times 10=20$\n$4 \\times 5=20$\nThe listed factor $5$ needs its partner $4$.\nThe missing factor is $4$.\nThe corrected list is $1,2,4,5,10,20$."
      }
    ],
